    "explanation": "To both parties: this is a rider-filed route-deviation dispute over trip TRP-00101 (Jurong East MRT to Marina Bay Sands, 12 July 2026).\n\nDeviation. The controlling distance is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00101), which POL-RD-01 makes govern over the rounded trip-record copy (27.2 km). The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 229 fixes at the 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s — so none of limbs (a) to (c) fires, and the rider's threshold excess is measured from it directly. The trace records 27.18 km against the booked optimal route of 21.0 km (EV-TRIP-00101), an excess of 6.18 km, or 29.43%. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment gates (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so a route deviation is ESTABLISHED, and the rider's POL-RD-08 burden is discharged (trip id TRP-00101 and the 10:21:05 pickup timestamp match across trace, trip record and fare breakdown). The excess does not reach either materiality threshold (8.0 km or 50%), so POL-RD-06 is not engaged and no driver-conduct referral arises; independently, driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 over 812 completed trips in 90 days, so no repeat pattern is established, and the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only and cannot be substituted.\n\nExculpation. Nothing excuses the deviation. The chat log (EV-CHAT-00101) contains no rider instruction to detour and no waypoint, so POL-RD-04 fails; both pickup and dropoff amendment timestamps are null, so POL-RD-05 fails; the fare is METERED, so POL-RD-11 does not apply; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 does not apply. The bundle's only traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00101-01) is MISSING with weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot run on the record; no party asserted an external queue, breakdown, closure or incident, and POL-RD-13 confirms the absent advisory does not convert into a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The driver's own in-app message ('sorry boss missed the exit, coming back now') and his counterparty statement are admissions that corroborate the deviation rather than excuse it.\n\nRefund. On a METERED fare, POL-RD-02 gives the arithmetic: charged_total = 35.64; recomputed_fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 21.0 km + 0.28 x 26.0 min) x 1.0 surge (read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 27.63; refund = 35.64 - 27.63 = 8.01, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 = SGD 8.05. That figure is the whole of the rider's monetary remedy: it is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so not NO_ACTION, and at 22.5% of charged_total it is far below the 90% full-refund share, so not FULL_REFUND. It is less than the SGD 10.00 contested. There is no ERP, toll or surcharge line to correct under POL-RD-09 (all totals are 0.00 and no gantry was charged), and any off-route ERP would in any event be comprehended in the POL-RD-02 figure rather than added on top of it.\n\nExecution. The monetary effect, SGD 8.05, exceeds the execution threshold of SGD 8.00, so this ruling issues but is not auto-executed; it is placed in the human queue for release under POL-GEN-05. Both parties retain the appeal route under POL-GEN-04.",
